about P as being fixed,

248
00:22:47,790 --> 00:22:49,690
but this is now for all other--

249
00:22:49,690 --> 00:22:52,270
for all partitions P star.

250
00:22:52,270 --> 00:22:56,970
So this is for all P star.

251
00:22:56,970 --> 00:23:00,010
But if it holds
for all, this is--

252
00:23:00,010 --> 00:23:02,730
sorry-- is less
than or equal to.

253
00:23:02,730 --> 00:23:06,710
If it holds for all, then
it-- also, this inequality,

254
00:23:06,710 --> 00:23:08,170
this is a fixed number.

255
00:23:08,170 --> 00:23:13,210
This means that this here is
a lower bound for this family.

256
00:23:13,210 --> 00:23:22,490
So this means that L f of P is
less than or equal to the inf

257
00:23:22,490 --> 00:23:23,360
of those guys.

258
00:23:30,270 --> 00:23:32,870
It's less than or
equal to the inf.

259
00:23:32,870 --> 00:23:35,350
But that here is just the--

260
00:23:35,350 --> 00:23:41,430
this here is by definition
the upper Riemann sum--

261
00:23:41,430 --> 00:23:42,800
or, rather, Riemann integral.

262
00:23:47,570 --> 00:23:48,890
But this is for each.

263
00:23:48,890 --> 00:23:51,210
So now you forget
about the P star.

264
00:23:51,210 --> 00:23:54,190
You have that this thing here
is less than that number.

265
00:23:54,190 --> 00:23:56,230
So this means that
this number here

266
00:23:56,230 --> 00:24:00,716
is an upper bound for
this whole family.

267
00:24:00,716 --> 00:24:04,750
So this means that also the
sup, the smallest upper bound,

268
00:24:04,750 --> 00:24:06,990
must be less than that.

269
00:24:06,990 --> 00:24:15,150
So this means that
the sup of L of f, p

270
00:24:15,150 --> 00:24:18,450
must be less than or
equal to this thing here.

271
00:24:21,810 --> 00:24:25,580
But the sup is by definition
the lower integral.

272
00:24:29,770 --> 00:24:31,530
So you always have--

273
00:24:31,530 --> 00:24:33,550
and this claim over here.

274
00:24:38,290 --> 00:24:44,890
So that's the first.

275
00:24:44,890 --> 00:24:53,450
So let's look at a
function that is--

276
00:24:53,450 --> 00:24:57,670
I added just a little bit,
if you find it interesting.

277
00:24:57,670 --> 00:24:59,290
I find it interesting,
but maybe you

278
00:24:59,290 --> 00:25:04,330
don't, but a little bit
about Riemann, that he died

279
00:25:04,330 --> 00:25:08,290
rather young of tuberculosis.

280
00:25:08,290 --> 00:25:12,413
But he had an incredible impact.

281
00:25:12,413 --> 00:25:13,330
He had an incredible--

282
00:25:13,330 --> 00:25:15,730
I mean, this is one
of his contributions.

283
00:25:15,730 --> 00:25:20,350
His first contribution
is he was a student

284
00:25:20,350 --> 00:25:26,750
of another really famous
mathematician, perhaps

285
00:25:26,750 --> 00:25:28,290
the most famous of all time--

286
00:25:28,290 --> 00:25:29,390
Gauss.

287
00:25:29,390 --> 00:25:35,550
And so at those times,
when you wrote your thesis,

288
00:25:35,550 --> 00:25:38,250
then you had like six
months to write your thesis.

289
00:25:46,950 --> 00:25:49,450
Formally, you couldn't
choose your subject,

290
00:25:49,450 --> 00:25:51,510
but it was always--

291
00:25:51,510 --> 00:25:54,130
anyway, you always got
permission to choose it.

292
00:25:54,130 --> 00:25:57,350
You had to give three
suggestions for something

293
00:25:57,350 --> 00:25:59,710
you would write your thesis on.

294
00:25:59,710 --> 00:26:01,350
But it was always--

295
00:26:01,350 --> 00:26:05,390
it was a unspoken rule
that your advisor always

296
00:26:05,390 --> 00:26:06,430
picked number one.

297
00:26:06,430 --> 00:26:07,570
And that's what you wanted.

298
00:26:07,570 --> 00:26:09,990
And then you could add
some other crazy stuff

299
00:26:09,990 --> 00:26:12,670
as two other suggestions.

300
00:26:12,670 --> 00:26:15,830
So Riemann had
three suggestions.

301
00:26:15,830 --> 00:26:21,330
And the third one, which he
had absolutely no idea about,

302
00:26:21,330 --> 00:26:27,010
was to make sense of
curvature in higher dimension.

303
00:26:27,010 --> 00:26:30,110
And so he just put it in there.

304
00:26:30,110 --> 00:26:33,130
He knew it wasn't
going to be selected.

305
00:26:33,130 --> 00:26:35,330
But actually, at
the time, this was

306
00:26:35,330 --> 00:26:37,250
what Gauss was interested in.

307
00:26:37,250 --> 00:26:39,430
And so Gauss said, to
hell with the rules.

308
00:26:39,430 --> 00:26:41,010
I'll pick number three.

309
00:26:41,010 --> 00:26:44,150
And so he had six months, and
nobody had figured this out.

310
00:26:44,150 --> 00:26:47,210
So Gauss is considered
by many the greatest

311
00:26:47,210 --> 00:26:50,370
mathematician of all time.

312
00:26:50,370 --> 00:26:53,010
But after six months,
actually, so Riemann

313
00:26:53,010 --> 00:26:55,930
came up with something
called the curvature tensor,

314
00:26:55,930 --> 00:26:59,290
which is this objects
in all dimensions.

315
00:26:59,290 --> 00:27:02,090
And that generalized
Gauss's work.

316
00:27:02,090 --> 00:27:06,090
And this lay the foundation
for general relativity

317
00:27:06,090 --> 00:27:14,770
that came many years later,
70 years or so later.

318
00:27:14,770 --> 00:27:16,970
So that was the Riemann's first.

319
00:27:16,970 --> 00:27:20,230
This is one of Riemann's
other contributions.

320
00:27:20,230 --> 00:27:23,990
And there are other things that
was only published a long time

321
00:27:23,990 --> 00:27:29,110
after his death that have
had a tremendous contribution

322
00:27:29,110 --> 00:27:31,070
in other areas.

323
00:27:31,070 --> 00:27:33,070
Anyway, so this is--

324
00:27:33,070 --> 00:27:36,450
so this was Riemann's way
of defining the integrals.

325
00:27:44,830 --> 00:27:48,312
Let me look at a function.

326
00:27:48,312 --> 00:27:49,770
So we talk about
that a little bit.

327
00:27:49,770 --> 00:27:52,770
But we didn't
actually define it.

328
00:27:52,770 --> 00:27:56,870
So here's an example
of a function

329
00:27:56,870 --> 00:27:59,870
that is not Riemann integrable.

330
00:27:59,870 --> 00:28:04,750
So it's a function defined
on the interval from 0 to 1,

331
00:28:04,750 --> 00:28:07,790
so it's bounded.

332
00:28:07,790 --> 00:28:18,970
And so the function is
f of x is equal to 1

333
00:28:18,970 --> 00:28:21,600
if x here is rational.

334
00:28:25,650 --> 00:28:28,190
And it's 0 otherwise.

335
00:28:35,258 --> 00:28:39,510
And so of course, this function
here is always between 0 and 1.

336
00:28:39,510 --> 00:28:42,610
So it's definitely bounded.

337
00:28:42,610 --> 00:28:45,190
But if you take
now any interval--

338
00:28:50,530 --> 00:29:03,950
so this here, so I claim here
f is not Riemann integrable.

339
00:29:13,290 --> 00:29:15,620
And so the thing is
that if you take--

340
00:29:19,070 --> 00:29:25,070
if you take a interval
like this and you

341
00:29:25,070 --> 00:29:34,610
take a subpartition like
that, and now you have that--

342
00:29:34,610 --> 00:29:39,070
and now you're looking
at one of these mi.

343
00:29:39,070 --> 00:29:41,770
So here, you have xi minus 1.

344
00:29:41,770 --> 00:29:44,910
And here you have xi.

345
00:29:44,910 --> 00:29:48,670
And so you're looking at mi.

346
00:29:48,670 --> 00:29:51,830
So this is some little
interval like this.

347
00:29:51,830 --> 00:29:55,070
But on any kind
of small interval,

348
00:29:55,070 --> 00:29:57,010
if it's really a
proper integral,

349
00:29:57,010 --> 00:29:58,510
if it's not just
a point but it's

350
00:29:58,510 --> 00:30:01,950
a proper integral--
interval, then there's

351
00:30:01,950 --> 00:30:04,790
always points that are
rational and always points

352
00:30:04,790 --> 00:30:06,150
that are not rational.

353
00:30:06,150 --> 00:30:10,950
So this means that this here,
this here, the sup here,

354
00:30:10,950 --> 00:30:17,930
would have to be 1, but
the inf here would be 0.

355
00:30:17,930 --> 00:30:20,080
And so this means that for the--

356
00:30:20,080 --> 00:30:22,030
so this is just any partition.

357
00:30:22,030 --> 00:30:24,250
And so this means that for--

358
00:30:24,250 --> 00:30:29,610
if you're looking at
the upper sum here,

359
00:30:29,610 --> 00:30:34,290
but it's now the sum of
these capital Mi delta xi.

360
00:30:34,290 --> 00:30:35,730
This here is 1.

361
00:30:35,730 --> 00:30:39,450
So it's just the sum of the
length of the small interval.

362
00:30:39,450 --> 00:30:43,730
But that's just one because the
whole interval is from 0 to 1.

363
00:30:43,730 --> 00:30:48,650
And likewise, for the
lower interval, lower sum,

364
00:30:48,650 --> 00:30:55,450
this is the sum here of
this small mi delta xi.

365
00:30:55,450 --> 00:30:56,970
These here are 0.

366
00:30:56,970 --> 00:30:58,790
So this whole thing here is 0.

367
00:31:01,730 --> 00:31:08,370
So you see that if you--
this is for all partitions.

368
00:31:08,370 --> 00:31:11,170
So this means that if you
take the infimum of this,

369
00:31:11,170 --> 00:31:12,290
you still get 1.

370
00:31:12,290 --> 00:31:15,510
And if you take the sup
of these still get 0.

371
00:31:15,510 --> 00:31:18,530
So those two numbers
are not the same.

372
00:31:18,530 --> 00:31:22,870
The lower and the upper Riemann
integrals are not the same.

373
00:31:22,870 --> 00:31:25,170
So the function is not
Riemann integrable.

374
00:31:32,430 --> 00:31:34,920
So now the next thing is--

375
00:31:38,390 --> 00:31:42,630
the next thing is-- so we
want to know which functions

376
00:31:42,630 --> 00:31:45,710
are Riemann integrable.

377
00:31:45,710 --> 00:31:49,950
And so here's a useful
little criteria.

378
00:31:49,950 --> 00:31:56,220
So lemma-- so you have a
function again that is bounded.

379
00:32:00,990 --> 00:32:08,170
Then f is Riemann integrable.

380
00:32:08,170 --> 00:32:11,210
And again, we
write it like this.

381
00:32:11,210 --> 00:32:20,770
So it's Riemann integrable if
for all epsilon greater than 0,

382
00:32:20,770 --> 00:32:40,850
there exists a partition P
so that the upper integral--

383
00:32:40,850 --> 00:32:46,390
upper sum-- sorry-- so that the
upper sum minus the lower sum--

384
00:32:46,390 --> 00:32:51,050
remember that this is always
bigger than the lower sum

385
00:32:51,050 --> 00:32:55,410
if this here is
less than epsilon.

386
00:32:55,410 --> 00:32:59,130
So if we want to check that a
function is Riemann integrable,

387
00:32:59,130 --> 00:33:01,890
then we just need to check
that for all epsilon,

388
00:33:01,890 --> 00:33:09,390
we can find a partition
with this property.

389
00:33:09,390 --> 00:33:13,830
And so this is a statement that
is if and only if-- so I should

390
00:33:13,830 --> 00:33:15,410
say if and only if--

391
00:33:18,430 --> 00:33:21,650
if and only if.

392
00:33:35,310 --> 00:33:37,030
So just try to prove that.

393
00:33:37,030 --> 00:33:40,790
And then we're going
to use this later on

394
00:33:40,790 --> 00:33:45,770
to prove that a lot of functions
are Riemann integrable.

395
00:33:50,190 --> 00:33:59,250
So suppose that f--

396
00:33:59,250 --> 00:34:03,530
so if f here is
Riemann integrable--

397
00:34:11,889 --> 00:34:14,290
so if it is Riemann
integrable, then we

398
00:34:14,290 --> 00:34:20,138
know that this lower
Riemann integral

399
00:34:20,138 --> 00:34:23,099
is equal to the upper
Riemann integral.

400
00:34:29,170 --> 00:34:32,210
This here was the sup
of all-- this here

401
00:34:32,210 --> 00:34:39,050
was the sup of all lower sums
for all-- over all partitions.

402
00:34:39,050 --> 00:34:48,170
And this here was the
inf of all upper sum,

403
00:34:48,170 --> 00:34:50,989
like that, over all partitions.

404
00:34:57,930 --> 00:35:08,550
So therefore, given
epsilon greater than 0,

405
00:35:08,550 --> 00:35:20,350
there exists a partition P1.

406
00:35:20,350 --> 00:35:20,850
Why?

407
00:35:20,850 --> 00:35:23,050
Because this here has a
sup over all partitions.

408
00:35:23,050 --> 00:35:31,870
So it means that there exists
a partition so that this lower

409
00:35:31,870 --> 00:35:46,010
sum here is bigger or equal to
this here minus epsilon over 2.

410
00:35:46,010 --> 00:35:49,010
It's just because it's a
sup of all these numbers.

411
00:35:49,010 --> 00:35:54,220
So there must exist one that
comes this close to the sup.

412
00:36:11,330 --> 00:36:24,410
Likewise, there exists
a partition P2--

413
00:36:24,410 --> 00:36:26,930
sorry-- this here should be P1.

414
00:36:26,930 --> 00:36:29,370
This is the sup over-- sorry.

415
00:36:29,370 --> 00:36:33,990
So there exists a
partition P2 so that the--

416
00:36:33,990 --> 00:36:39,290
so that for that, this is
one where this value here

417
00:36:39,290 --> 00:36:40,270
is really small.

418
00:36:40,270 --> 00:36:43,670
So this is not too
much larger than this.

419
00:36:43,670 --> 00:36:54,370
So this means that this for
P2 is smaller or equal to this

420
00:36:54,370 --> 00:37:02,870
here, upper Riemann integral
plus epsilon over 2.

421
00:37:09,470 --> 00:37:32,750
So now let P be the partition
with all the dividing points

422
00:37:32,750 --> 00:37:40,130
of both P1 and P2.

423
00:37:40,130 --> 00:37:43,470
So it has all of the
dividing points from P1

424
00:37:43,470 --> 00:37:46,936
together with all of the
dividing points from P2.

425
00:37:46,936 --> 00:37:50,910
But now for this
partition, we have that--

426
00:37:50,910 --> 00:37:55,310
well, for-- this is
a refinement of P1.

427
00:37:55,310 --> 00:37:58,610
So if it's refinement,
the value here goes up.

428
00:38:03,330 --> 00:38:06,370
And this thing here is--

429
00:38:06,370 --> 00:38:11,730
so this is less than the
upper for the same thing.

430
00:38:11,730 --> 00:38:15,610
And since it's a
refinement also of P2,

431
00:38:15,610 --> 00:38:20,150
we have that it is less
than the upper sum for P2.

432
00:38:23,530 --> 00:38:28,210
But now you see that
this thing here--

433
00:38:28,210 --> 00:38:32,750
so L-- so the difference
between these two--

434
00:38:32,750 --> 00:38:35,330
the difference between
these two numbers--

435
00:38:35,330 --> 00:38:37,470
so this is the difference here.

436
00:38:37,470 --> 00:38:45,610
So U f P minus U f P-- sorry--

437
00:38:45,610 --> 00:38:51,870
L f P, this difference here,
this is bigger than that.

438
00:38:51,870 --> 00:38:54,050
So if you take this
and subtract this,

439
00:38:54,050 --> 00:38:56,210
you're getting
something non-negative.

440
00:38:56,210 --> 00:38:59,190
And this, the spread
between these two,

441
00:38:59,190 --> 00:39:02,110
is smaller than the
spread between these.

442
00:39:02,110 --> 00:39:10,520
So this is less than U
of f P2 minus L of f P1.

443
00:39:13,030 --> 00:39:16,750
But this thing here is--

444
00:39:16,750 --> 00:39:25,590
this thing here is less than U
f P2 minus this upper integral

445
00:39:25,590 --> 00:39:26,090
here.

446
00:39:30,190 --> 00:39:31,890
Assuming that it's
Riemann integral,

447
00:39:31,890 --> 00:39:34,230
so the upper and
lower are the same.

448
00:39:34,230 --> 00:39:47,870
So this thing here we can write
it as this plus minus L f P1

449
00:39:47,870 --> 00:39:56,730
minus the integral
here, like that.

450
00:39:56,730 --> 00:40:02,920
I'm just subtracting and then
adding back the same thing.

451
00:40:02,920 --> 00:40:06,320
And this one here, we
already found that this here

452
00:40:06,320 --> 00:40:10,780
was bounded by epsilon over 2.

453
00:40:10,780 --> 00:40:12,880
This here is--
remember, we're assuming

454
00:40:12,880 --> 00:40:15,020
that it's Riemann integrable.

455
00:40:15,020 --> 00:40:20,640
So this here is the same thing
as when you have the upper one.

456
00:40:20,640 --> 00:40:24,000
And this thing here is--

457
00:40:24,000 --> 00:40:29,180
this here is also bounded
by-- this is actually right.

458
00:40:29,180 --> 00:40:33,700
This is negative, but it's--

459
00:40:33,700 --> 00:40:40,680
so this thing here is
bigger or equal to--

460
00:40:40,680 --> 00:40:42,070
maybe I should write it as--

461
00:40:45,600 --> 00:40:48,280
well, let me write
it like this-- plus.

462
00:40:48,280 --> 00:40:51,680
And then I can write it
as the integral from a

463
00:40:51,680 --> 00:40:59,820
to b of f of x dx
minus L f of P1.

464
00:40:59,820 --> 00:41:04,420
But this thing here was
bounded by epsilon over 2 also.

465
00:41:04,420 --> 00:41:08,020
So epsilon over 2
plus epsilon over 2.

466
00:41:08,020 --> 00:41:10,900
So this is equal to epsilon.

467
00:41:15,940 --> 00:41:21,460
So again, if you want to test
that a function is Riemann

468
00:41:21,460 --> 00:41:24,560
integral, you just need
to find-- for a given,

469
00:41:24,560 --> 00:41:26,620
for any given epsilon,
you need to be

470
00:41:26,620 --> 00:41:32,740
able to find a partition so that
the upper sum for that partition

471
00:41:32,740 --> 00:41:37,540
is minus the lower sum
for the same partition

472
00:41:37,540 --> 00:41:38,680
is less than epsilon.

473
00:41:42,495 --> 00:41:47,740
And so now this leads
us to the next theorem.

474
00:41:47,740 --> 00:41:52,920
So the next theorem is that
any continuous function

475
00:41:52,920 --> 00:41:54,580
is Riemann integrable.

476
00:42:07,280 --> 00:42:09,240
So any Riemann sum--

477
00:42:09,240 --> 00:42:10,840
so any continuous function--

478
00:42:20,480 --> 00:42:26,600
any continuous function on an
integral like this-- this is--

479
00:42:26,600 --> 00:42:30,235
a and b are real numbers--

480
00:42:30,235 --> 00:42:33,180
it is Riemann integrable.

481
00:42:41,800 --> 00:42:45,480
So this is the next theorem
that we want to prove.

482
00:42:45,480 --> 00:42:48,720
But in order to prove
that, we need a tool.

483
00:42:48,720 --> 00:42:52,800
And so this is what's
called uniformly continuous.

484
00:42:56,620 --> 00:42:59,260
So just to show this,
we need the notion

485
00:42:59,260 --> 00:43:03,420
of being uniformly continuous.

486
00:43:03,420 --> 00:43:06,500
So what is that?

487
00:43:06,500 --> 00:43:30,600
So in the proof, we need the
notion of uniformly continuous.

488
00:43:39,820 --> 00:43:42,260
So that's the following.

489
00:43:42,260 --> 00:43:47,060
And you have a function
defined on some interval, say.

490
00:43:47,060 --> 00:43:51,720
It could be all of
R, for that matter.

491
00:43:51,720 --> 00:43:54,440
So you have a
function like this.

492
00:43:54,440 --> 00:43:58,200
And f is said to be--

493
00:43:58,200 --> 00:44:21,480
is said to be uniformly
continuous if for all epsilon

494
00:44:21,480 --> 00:44:31,000
greater than 0, there
exists delta greater than 0

495
00:44:31,000 --> 00:44:39,200
such that as long as x and
y are less than delta, then

496
00:44:39,200 --> 00:44:48,344
their images is
less than epsilon.

497
00:44:48,344 --> 00:44:52,120
